== 6. Addendum, 4 Nov: Vivado runner fix (issue of 4 Nov)
Symptom on Vivado 2024.2 (Windows): xsim printed its option list, "Expected a switch but found 1"; no simulation ran.
Cause: xsim.bat splits arguments at '=', so "--testplusarg SEED=1" arrived as "SEED" and "1".
Fix: run.tcl passes such options through an options file (xsim <snapshot> --file simulate.args).
Also fixed: two xelab warnings (XSIM 43-3373) from void'($value$plusargs()) in tb_pkg.sv.
Check here: an xsim stub that splits arguments the way a batch file does reproduces the failure with the old run.tcl,
and the new run.tcl gives:
tb_rr_arbiter        U01          PASS  checks=310493 errors=0
tb_sync_fifo         U02          PASS  checks=196864 errors=0
tb_route_compute     U03          PASS  checks=856450 errors=0
Testbench lint after the tb_pkg change: clean. Seed-1 counts unchanged. Bundles regenerated and rebuilt (U02 PASS, 196,864).
The real Vivado run is the proof: R-1105-xx.
